 "methods": {
  "re-nma-pm-kh": "Random-effects fit at edge level. Per edge: Elo difference y = 400*log10(p/(1-p)) (three players, one against two: 400*log10(2p/(1-p))) with p = (points + prior)/(games + 1), standard error clustered over opening pairs or openings (binomial for totals-only edges). Weighted least squares over all edges of the scale with weights 1/(se^2 + tau^2); tau (between-edge standard deviation, Elo) by the Paule-Mandel estimator; half-width = t(df, 0.975) * standard error against the anchor (Knapp-Hartung quantile). Check: leave-one-edge-out 95 % prediction intervals cover 47 of 49 (2p-adj-r5), 16 of 16 (2p-adj-r4), 31 of 32 (3p-adj-r4) edges; the fixed-effect model covers 20 of 49, 10 of 16, 22 of 32.",
  "direct-match": "Elo difference of one head-to-head match, 400*log10(p/(1-p)), interval from that match alone (docs/training.md). Describes this pairing only.",
  "bt-mle-bootstrap": "Bradley-Terry maximum likelihood with cluster bootstrap over openings (scripts/elo/fit.py, tier1/ratings.json). Intervals contain sampling error only; rejected as published interval because the model does not fit (deviance p 0.005 to 0.010)."
 },
